                               Fault 4 - VLANs 50 and 60 removed from the trunk

Symptom:

PC-SEC (VLAN 50, 192.168.50.10) could not ping its gateway at 192.168.50.1. All 4 packets timed out.

What I did to break it:

On SW1-CORE, on the trunk port going to SW2 (Gi0/1), I cut the allowed VLAN list down.

    SW1-CORE(config)# interface gigabitEthernet0/1
    SW1-CORE(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30,40

Commands used to diagnose:

    SW1-CORE# show interfaces trunk

The allowed list for Gi0/1 only went up to 40. VLANs 50 and 60 were missing.

Root cause:

Since 50 and 60 were not allowed on the trunk, SW1 dropped all frames tagged for those VLANs. PC-SEC is on SW2, so its traffic has to cross that trunk to get to the router, and it never got there. The cable and the trunk were both still up, which makes this one easy to miss because the link looks fine but is missing VLANs.

Fix:

    SW1-CORE> enable
    SW1-CORE# configure terminal
    SW1-CORE(config)# interface gigabitEthernet0/1
    SW1-CORE(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30,40,50,60
    SW1-CORE(config-if)# end
    SW1-CORE# write memory

Verification:

I ran show interfaces trunk again to check all six VLANs were listed, then pinged the gateway from PC-SEC.

    C:\> ping 192.168.50.1

    Pinging 192.168.50.1 with 32 bytes of data:
    Reply from 192.168.50.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255
    Reply from 192.168.50.1: bytes=32 time=10ms TTL=255
    Reply from 192.168.50.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255
    Reply from 192.168.50.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255

